Z||000000||PatrickB||10-15-2000||07:27 PM||||I was recently looking in my engine cleaning all the ground wires and I found one that wasnt connected.  It looks like the previous owner might have disconnected it and it was folded up and tucked back so you cant see it.  Anyway I was wondering if someone could tell me where it connects to.  It is a copper braided wire just to the left of the battery.  There are three connections their and this one is the one all the way on the bottom.  Could someone tell me where the other side connects to?<P>Thanks, <BR> Patrick||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||10-15-2000||08:21 PM||||Is it a bare flat copper wire? It hooks to the bottem bolt where the rear decklid bolts onto the car, on the pass. side.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
